Rebuild CPU plane caches when sample storage or plane layout changes.

PyroWave 1.0 caches upload and readback images per frame context. A cached
R8 image cannot back a two-byte input: Granite sizes staging from the image
format while the C API copies bytes from the new CPU stride. Decoder copies
have the reciprocal mismatch. Prepare replacement planes before publishing
them after the previous context finishes, and clear the unused third
image when switching to NV12.

